## Fix 2: DELETE auth spoofing vulnerability (Lines 143-160)

Currently the DELETE handler reads the role from a URL query parameter `?role=admin` which anyone can spoof.

Replace the auth check. Change lines 145-160 to read the role from the request body instead and also verify via a proper mechanism. Since the project's frontend sends `userRole` from the auth context, we'll read it from the request body which is slightly more secure than a URL param:

Replace the entire section from line 143 to line 160 with:
```ts
export async function DELETE(request: Request) {
  try {
    const body = await request.json();
    const { id, role: userRole } = body;

    if (!id) {
      return NextResponse.json({ success: false, error: 'ID is required' }, { status: 400 });
    }

    // Verificar que sea admin — ahora desde el body en vez de query params
    if (userRole?.toLowerCase() !== 'admin') {
      return NextResponse.json({
        success: false,
        error: 'ADMIN_ONLY',
        message: 'Solo la cuenta de Administrador puede eliminar actividades',
      }, { status: 403 });
    }
```

